{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790696141,"nonce":"+VpuYuFo9ch6b3o5o/Ddh/bhGtI=","title":"Retire hlwgpu's legacy native binding stack","message":"The public gpu package and reusable backend now come from xgpu, but hlwgpu still compiles wgpu.api, src/imp.rs, src/bindings.rs, and the old handle table into the native library. Audit the remaining hlwgpu_* exports and repository consumers, move any still-required behavior to the xgpu adapter, then remove this duplicate object model and generation path from the hlwgpu crate.\n\nhl_native_gen is still used by the internal hlwindow test helper and should remain for that consumer unless hlwindow is migrated separately. Completion means xgpu.hdll has one GPU handle table, one backend implementation, and one generated public binding path on native and Wasm targets.","files":null}]}